Parses `.steno` source files into a typed AST — specifically, turns raw text into `Vec<Entry>`, with each entry's template parsed to `Vec<Chunk>`. This is stage 1 of the pipeline; it does not expand counts, compile movement, or emit JSON.

`Chunk` represents a single template node: literal text, control flow (`Repeat` with separator and body, `Landing` / `Computed` / `EndLanding` for positioning), or special markers (`Dcount`, `TypeSlot`, `FusedTypeSlot`, `BodyBreak`, `Pattern`). `Expr` encodes computed indices as `a*d + b` (where `d` is the repeat index). `Entry` holds the parsed result: stroke sequence, template chunks, raw text, optional `@count` spec and `@arity`, and `EntryFlags` for `@multiline`, `@type`, `@noarg`, `@fuse`, `@literal`.

`EntryFlags::set_named` is the only writer to flags and must stay in sync with the directive parser in `expr.rs`. `Chunk::kind_name` returns the DSL tag used in error messages and diagnostics — the string must match the design docs exactly. `FusedTypeSlot` is only emitted by the programmatic corpus path (`dict.infinite.steno`); `dict.steno` never uses it.

Public entry points are `parse_source(text) -> Result<Vec<Entry>>` and `parse_template(text) -> Result<Vec<Chunk>>`, delegated to `source.rs` and `template.rs`.